OBS id=LEAD :: Two Claude sessions ran after the reboot. The second one (WT tab) rewrote §49 into the assignment list now in that file and did not wake you. The user closed it; I (p1) am the only lead now. §49 as it stands on disk is valid: do its FIX-M1, FIX-M2, FIX-L1, FIX-L2, FIX-L3 and FIX-L5, and keep its DEFER list. The edit freeze from §47 ends now for these items only.
ASG id=FIX-M3 pri=1 :: src/plugins/agentcmd.rs:130-135 managed() requires marker revision == REVISION. After a future REVISION bump, rerunning `crew plugin agentcmd install` makes preflight treat all existing agentcmd.* modules as unrelated plugins and abort. Accept any marker with kind == "crew-managed-agentcmd", let the new install supersede the old revision, and keep each module's enabled state. Add a unit test with a marker that has an older revision.
ASG id=FIX-L4 :: src/plugins/path_dirs.rs:95-105 test fixture `c.incompatible` puts `platforms=[...]` after `[[path_dirs]]`, so TOML assigns it to the path_dirs table, not the plugin. Put the plugin-level platforms line before the table, and assert that entries() reports platform_compatible == false for it and that collect() skips it.
ASG id=FIX-L6 :: src/server.rs:436-451 when the base env has no PATH, PATH becomes only the plugin dirs. In that case do not set PATH; record a diagnostic instead. Add a unit test if the helper is testable without a pane.
ASG id=P5-FLAKE :: tests/pane_host_lost.rs live_host_is_not_reported_lost_when_helper_exits failed 2 of 4 runs on this branch (wait-output P5_TEST_STILL_ALIVE timeout at :92 via :314) and passed 11 of 11 on main ad5024b. Find out whether the branch causes it (for example the extra prepare() IO or the PATH change slowing pane startup) or whether it is the C-c then immediate `pane run` race at :307-313. Show evidence with repeated runs on both main and the branch. Fix the root cause; if it is only the test race, wait for the prompt after C-c before `pane run`.
